{
  "uid": "broker-spike",
  "title": "Broker Spike — Kafka vs RabbitMQ",
  "tags": [
    "spike",
    "broker",
    "adr"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "5s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-15m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this dashboard is for",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Evidence for **docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-14-broker-kafka-vs-rabbitmq.md**. Targets only exist while `infra/broker-spike/compose.yaml` is up and `prometheus-brokers.yml` is in `infra/observability/prometheus/scrape/`.\n\nThe asymmetry is the point: **RabbitMQ's panels come from the broker itself** (`rabbitmq_prometheus`, enabled by default, 231 broker metrics). **Kafka's come from a `kafka-exporter` sidecar** that exposes 16 — broker internals (heap, GC, request queues) would need a second mechanism, the JMX exporter."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Backlog — the 'are events flowing' signal",
      "description": "RabbitMQ reports queue depth directly. Kafka's lag is derived by the sidecar, and MUST be filtered with `> 0`: kafka_consumergroup_lag returns -1 for partitions with no committed offset, so a bare sum() under-reports by 1 per idle partition.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rabbitmq_queue_messages_ready)",
          "legendFormat": "rabbitmq — messages ready",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(kafka_consumergroup_lag > 0)",
          "legendFormat": "kafka — consumer lag (filtered)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "sum(kafka_consumergroup_lag)",
          "legendFormat": "kafka — bare sum() (WRONG, shown to prove it)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Broker memory",
      "description": "RabbitMQ self-reports RSS. Kafka has no equivalent here — the sidecar cannot see inside the JVM, which is exactly why the ADR budgets Kafka from `podman stats` instead.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "rabbitmq_process_resident_memory_bytes",
          "legendFormat": "rabbitmq RSS (self-reported)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "RabbitMQ — publish vs acknowledge rate",
      "description": "Publishes climbing while acks stay flat is a stalled consumer. This pair is free with the built-in plugin.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "rate(rabbitmq_global_messages_received_total[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "received/s",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "rate(rabbitmq_global_messages_acknowledged_total[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "acknowledged/s",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Kafka — write rate per partition",
      "description": "Derived from the topic's end offset moving. Uneven lines across partitions mean the partition key is skewed — the thing that actually breaks per-key ordering at scale.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 13
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "rate(kafka_topic_partition_current_offset{topic!~\"__.*\"}[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "{{topic}} p{{partition}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Metrics the broker gives you about ITSELF",
      "description": "Counted from the scrape, not from documentation. Two-thirds of Kafka's endpoint is the exporter's own Go runtime.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "count(count by (__name__)({job=\"rabbitmq\"}))",
          "legendFormat": "rabbitmq",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "count(count by (__name__)({job=\"kafka\"}))",
          "legendFormat": "kafka (via sidecar)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Scrape health — both targets",
      "description": "If a line drops to 0 the spike stack is down; remove prometheus-brokers.yml from the scrape dir rather than leaving a dead target.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 21
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "max": 1,
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "up{job=~\"kafka|rabbitmq\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{job}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      }
    }
  ],
  "version": 1
}
